  m_text: Male platypuses have venomous spurs on their back legs, which makes them
    one of the very few venomous mammals. The venom isn't deadly to humans, but it
    can cause terrible pain. Males mostly use their spurs when competing with other
    males during breeding season. Please admire platypuses from a distance!
