      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The platypus is a monotreme, a special group of mammals that is neither
    a marsupial (like a kangaroo) nor a placental mammal (like a dog). It has fur
    and feeds its babies milk, but it has some very unusual features, like a duck-like
    bill and a beaver-like tail. Only five monotreme species exist in the world:
    the platypus and four types of echidna. It''s not a reptile either, even though
    it can seem like a mix of different animals!'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
