  m_text: A baby platypus is called a puggle. Puggles are tiny when they hatch, about
    the size of a jellybean, and are fed milk by their mum in a cosy burrow for several
    months. They stay safe underground until they're big enough to swim and find
    food. (Your puggle photo would fit perfectly here!)
